          parameters:
            createpointprim: false
            numpoints: 50
            normal: none
          flags:
          - viewer
          position: [-1425, -75]
        - name: ramp1_keys
          type: tableDAT
          flags:
          - viewer
          - -showDocked
          position: [900, -395]
          size: [130, 90]
          dock: ramp1
          dat_content:
          - - pos
            - r
            - g
            - b
            - a
          - - '0'
            - '0'
            - '0'
            - '0'
            - '1'
          - - '0.09898477'
            - '1'
            - '0.45'
            - '0'
            - '1'
          - - '0.25136903'
            - '1'
            - '0'
            - '0'
            - '1'
          - - '0.4899477'
            - '1'
            - '0'
            - '0'
            - '1'
          - - '0.65492237'
            - '0.62431663'
            - '0'
            - '0.797'
            - '1'
          - - '1'
            - '0'
            - '0.049999952'
            - '1'
            - '1'
          dat_content_format: table
        - name: rectangle1
          type: rectanglePOP
          parameters:
            surftype: lines
            scale: 1.81
          position: [175, -150]
        - name: transform1
          type: transformTOP
          parameters:
            bgcolora: 1
            compover: true
          position: [1475, -75]
          size: [130, 90]
          color: [0.67, 0.67, 0.67]
          inputs:
          - render1
        - name: linemetrics1
          type: linemetricsPOP
          parameters:
            dispprev: true
            diststartnorm: true
            distendnorm: true
          flags:
          - viewer
          position: [-475, -75]
          size: [130, 90]
          color: [0.67, 0.67, 0.67]
          inputs:
          - lineresample1
        - name: mathcombine1
          type: mathcombinePOP
          sequences:
            comb:
            - summary: =me.curBlock.summary
              oper: mult
              scopea: DistStartNorm
              scopeb: DistEndNorm
              result: PointScale
            post:
            - scope: PointScale
              fromhigh0: 0.25
              tolow0: 0.001
              result: PointScale
          flags:
          - viewer
          position: [-100, -75]
          inputs:
          - linemetrics1
        - name: lineresample1
          type: lineresamplePOP
          parameters:
            resamplemethod: linestrip
            resampledivs: 30
          flags:
          - viewer
          position: [-775, -75]
          size: [130, 90]
          color: [0.67, 0.67, 0.67]
          inputs:
          - trail1
        annotations:
        - name: annotate1
          mode: annotate
          title: Create movement
          text: We use a noise to create random movement on the points
          position: [-1237, -200]
          size: [207, 343]
          color: [0.45, 0.45, 0.45]
        - name: annotate2
          mode: annotate
          title: Trail the points
          text: Creates line strips along the points movements
          position: [-1000, -200]
          size: [178, 348]
          color: [0.45, 0.45, 0.45]
        - name: annotate3
          mode: annotate
          title: Resample line strips
          text: Here we setup a specified amount of points for each line strip
          position: [-800, -200]
          size: [207, 348]
          color: [0.45, 0.45, 0.45]
        - name: annotate4
          mode: annotate
          title: Get line strips data
          text: |-
            Linemetrics gives us here 3 attributes :

            - DistStartNorm : normalized distance (between 0 and 1) between each points and the beginning of the associated line
            - DistEndNorm : normalized distance (between 0 and 1) between each points and the end of the associated line
            - DispPrev : direction towards the previous point in the line strip
          position: [-550, -200]
          size: [305, 459]
          color: [0.45, 0.45, 0.45]
        - name: annotate5
          mode: annotate
          title: PointScale according to point position in line
          text: "Here we multiply DistStartNorm and DistEndNorm in order to have a maximum Scale in the middle of the line. \nMultiplying these two attributes gives us a maximum value of 0.25 in the middle of the line so we post multiply the result x4 to have a 0 to 1 PointScale.\nAlso, if you check the Math Combine 'Post' page, 'Map to Low' isn't pure 0 because otherwise the normals calculations can go wrong. Try to put 0, you will see :)"
          position: [-200, -200]
          size: [328, 479]
          color: [0.45, 0.45, 0.45]
        - name: annotate7
          mode: annotate
          title: Skin !!!
          text: Here we skin primitives every N groups. The value of N is the number of Divisions we set in the Line Resample POP + 1. If we don't choose this operation, the Skin POP can behave in a "chaotic" way
          position: [575, -200]
          size: [207, 404]
          color: [0.45, 0.45, 0.45]
        - name: annotate8
          mode: annotate
          title: Not useful, just visualization
          text: |2-







            I use these CHOPs just to show you "what's happening" in the LineMetrics and MathCombine POPs
          position: [-549, -427]
          size: [677, 188]
          color: [0.45, 0.45, 0.45]
        - name: annotate9
          mode: annotate
          title: Copy circle
          text: |-
            We copy circle1 according to the PointScale we calculated and we choose to rotate each circle according to 'DispPrev'.
            aggiungere slider apc su uniform scale range 0.2-10 e number copies 2-20
          position: [350, -200]
          size: [207, 352]
          color: [0.45, 0.45, 0.45]
